From eac73153d19b234bc00979037cff17c964b21a49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: No <No@ty.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 19:12:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(tts): add OpenAI-compatible TTS client for
 self-hosted speech servers

Adds an 'openai-tts' TTSClient targeting any OpenAI-compatible speech
server (e.g. a patched macos-speech-server, kokoro-fastapi):

- src/libs/openaiTTS.ts: fetch layer using Tauri plugin-http on native
  platforms (bypasses webview CORS). Health check via GET /v1/models
  (3s timeout), voice catalog via /v1/audio/voices/all with fallback to
  the flat /v1/audio/voices list (Apple/Kokoro id inference), speech via
  POST /v1/audio/speech (WAV, always speed 1.0). LRU blob cache keyed by
  the full payload (model+text+voice+response_format+speed) with
  in-flight dedup; AbortSignal + timeouts on every request; endpoint
  normalization accepts trailing slashes and an optional /v1 suffix;
  optional Bearer API key.
- src/services/tts/OpenAITTSClient.ts: mirrors EdgeTTSClient's playback
  pipeline (SSML marks -> per-sentence WAV -> silence trim -> WSOLA
  time-stretch -> gapless WebAudioPlayer scheduling with audible-chunk
  boundary events, retry with 4xx skip-not-fail, measured-duration
  recording). Sentence granularity only; no word boundaries.
- TTSController: registers the client (init succeeds only when an
  endpoint is configured AND the server answers the health check),
  merges its voice group into the picker, routes setVoice to it, and
  extends the section-timeline/scrubber gate to any client with an
  audio clock.
- Settings: ReadSettings.openaiTtsEndpoint / openaiTtsApiKey with
  defaults, editable in Settings -> TTS (new OpenAI-Compatible TTS
  boxed list), persisted like all global settings.
- Tests for endpoint normalization and voice-id inference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
